# Pàdéyá project rules

## Scope discipline

- Do not implement future phases unless explicitly requested.
- Do not rebuild the old Pàdéyá marketing website.
- Auth, events, payments, tickets, Legacy Page, Vault, and AI stay out of scope until asked.
- Prefer small, focused files. Do not create giant files.

## Secrets & config

- Do not hardcode secrets.
- Use environment variables and `.env.example` files only.
- Never commit real credentials, API keys, or webhook secrets.

## Backend

- Keep the FastAPI backend modular by domain (`app/auth`, `app/events`, etc.).
- Add tests for important backend logic.
- Use audit logs for admin and finance actions.
- Do not trust frontend payment success.
- Only issue tickets after a verified payment webhook.
- Use signed QR payloads for tickets/check-in.
- Manual payouts require immutable evidence.

## Frontend

- Keep components reusable and small.
- Use centralized brand tokens (`src/lib/brand.ts` + CSS variables).
- Do not hardcode random colors in components — use brand tokens / Tailwind theme colors.
- Use official logo assets from `frontend/public/brand/`.
  - Dark-background logo on black/dark surfaces.
  - Light-background logo on white/light surfaces.
- Do not recreate the logo with text.

## Permissions (product invariants)

- Hosts cannot delete reviews.
- Support cannot modify financial records.
- Manual payouts require immutable evidence.
- Messaging: fan↔host rules stay fan↔host; fan↔fan is Fan Connect connection-only; pins are shared per thread; stars are private to the viewer; replies are same-thread and permission-checked via `app.messaging.permissions`.

## Lifecycle (product invariant)

- CRUD/lifecycle is never optional for product modules.
- Every current and future module must have a complete lifecycle plan in `docs/CRUD_MATRIX.md` (create, read, update, end-of-life, restore, permissions, audit, FE, tests).
- Intentionally read-only or append-only resources (payments, ledger, audit logs, evidence) still need an explicit plan — document *system-only / immutable / reverse-only* and enforce it.
- Prefer archive/cancel/deactivate over hard delete. Follow `docs/CRUD_PATTERN.md`.
